1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,040
What is the biggest misconception that you feel people have about Black resistance?

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:07,680
That it's criminal.

3
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:14,880
That any time you see someone engaged in defiance, what they are doing is illegal.

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:18,420
And needs to be, like, prosecuted to the full extent of the law.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,820
Or that if it's not criminalized, it's immoral.

6
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,660
Oh, we shouldn't be doing this.

7
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,600
You know, yeah, that's what happens.

8
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,320
Black resistance gets a bad rap.

9
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:32,420
What's one thing you said in this episode that you stand 10 toes down on?

10
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,300
Coalition building.

11
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:35,980
I think coalition building is so important.

12
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,740
We cannot do this work alone.

13
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:39,600
We cannot do this work in isolation.

14
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:41,960
It is an all-hands-on-death approach.

15
